WEBVTT

00:00.180 --> 00:01.170
Instructor: The next GitHub feature

00:01.170 --> 00:02.910
we'll cover are gists.

00:02.910 --> 00:05.490
So GitHub gists are a very simple way

00:05.490 --> 00:07.080
to share code snippets.

00:07.080 --> 00:09.780
If you're familiar with something called pastebin

00:09.780 --> 00:11.250
it's a very similar tool.

00:11.250 --> 00:14.040
It allows you to basically copy some code

00:14.040 --> 00:17.130
into a gist and then save that

00:17.130 --> 00:20.070
and share it with other people or refer back to it later.

00:20.070 --> 00:23.100
You don't have access to all the GitHub repo features

00:23.100 --> 00:24.930
but you have access to some of them,

00:24.930 --> 00:26.910
like forking, for example.

00:26.910 --> 00:28.470
So I'll just demonstrate it,

00:28.470 --> 00:30.990
first to access gist, not over there,

00:30.990 --> 00:35.990
over here, if you go to GitHub, I go to gist.github.com.

00:36.480 --> 00:39.840
Now, I'm sure there's a button somewhere.

00:39.840 --> 00:41.910
I think it's actually, if we go here

00:41.910 --> 00:45.030
to your profile and then your gists

00:45.030 --> 00:47.070
I think that's the easiest way to get there.

00:47.070 --> 00:48.450
Maybe there's another way

00:48.450 --> 00:51.900
without just typing gists.github.com.

00:51.900 --> 00:54.450
So it's a different page, right?

00:54.450 --> 00:58.770
We see my personal list of gists actually,

00:58.770 --> 01:01.170
I don't use them very frequently on this account.

01:01.170 --> 01:03.870
