04:54.270 --> 04:56.970
and that's kind of all that there is to gists.

04:56.970 --> 05:00.540
So this one again, is secret, it's private

05:00.540 --> 05:01.800
but I could make a new gist

05:01.800 --> 05:05.310
and instead just make it public here.

05:05.310 --> 05:07.295
And anybody could see that on my account.

05:07.295 --> 05:10.860
And anybody can see anybody else's public gist.

05:10.860 --> 05:13.740
As you saw here, there's this discovery feature.

05:13.740 --> 05:16.110
I never, ever really use this

05:16.110 --> 05:19.380
I guess except for this video where I'm showing you it.

05:19.380 --> 05:21.330
It's pretty rare that I just wanna stumble across

05:21.330 --> 05:22.830
random gists.

05:22.830 --> 05:25.860
Anyway, that's all there is to GitHub gists.

05:25.860 --> 05:27.120
You can have multiple files,

05:27.120 --> 05:29.490
different file types, different extensions.

05:29.490 --> 05:31.770
You can share them, you can keep them secret.

05:31.770 --> 05:33.240
They are, I believe

05:33.240 --> 05:36.010
behind the scenes actual Git repositories

05:36.960 --> 05:39.030
although they don't expose the same features

05:39.030 --> 05:41.040
on GitHub that we normally have access

05:41.040 --> 05:43.050
to with a full fledged repo.

05:43.050 --> 05:46.140
But we can see revisions, we can see diffs.

05:46.140 --> 05:47.700
So there is a history here

05:47.700 --> 05:49.500
but they're just very slimmed down

05:49.500 --> 05:52.050
the actual interface is very streamlined compared

05:52.050 --> 05:53.850
to a full GitHub repository.

05:53.850 --> 05:56.483
So that about wraps it up for GitHub Gists.
